  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4203.07 Lacquers",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4203.07 Lacquers. Notwithstanding Env-A 4203.01, any person or facility may add up to 10 percent by volume of VOC to a lacquer to avoid blushing of the finish during days with relative humidity greater than 70 percent and temperature below 65°F at the time of application, provided that the coating contains acetone and no more than 550 grams of VOC per liter of coating, less water and exempt compounds, prior to the addition of VOC.\n\nSource. #8695, eff 7-27-06; ss by #10736, eff 1-1-15; ss by #14202, eff 2-26-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4200.html"
